## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to plan complex platform migrations under real constraints, balancing reliability, regulatory needs, and delivery velocity.

## Key Concepts
- Phased migration with pilots and dual write to reduce risk
- Dependency mapping and data contracts across squads
- Cutover strategy (canary/blue‑green) and rollback plan
- Observability, SLO enforcement, auditability, and data-retention alignment

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: determine rollout phase and guardrails
function migratePhase(phase) {
  if (phase === 'pilot') startPilot();
  else if (phase === 'staged') startStagedRollout();
  else if (phase === 'full') startFullCutover();
  else throw new Error('Unknown phase');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- What metrics determine promotion from pilot to staged rollout?
- How would you mitigate Pulsar vendor lock-in risks and ensure exit paths?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests ability to design governance for cross-team experimentation, balancing speed with reliability and data integrity.

## Key Concepts
- KPI ownership and charter
- Preflight power analysis and data-quality gates
- Guardrails: latency, error rate, quotas
- Feature flags, canary and cohort rollouts
- Artifacts: experiment charter, data map, rollback plan

## Code Example
```javascript
function shouldRollout(experiment, metrics) {
  const {power, mde, dataQuality} = metrics;
  if (!experiment.flagsEnabled) return false;
  if (power < experiment.requiredPower) return false;
  if (!dataQuality.ok) return false;
  if (metrics.latency > experiment.maxLatency) return false;
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would thresholds vary by product area?
- How would you measure guardrail impact on velocity and reliability?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to triage, harden reliability under pressure, and coordinate cross-team remediation with business impact.

## Key Concepts

- Incident containment and rollback
- Safe fallbacks, circuit breakers, backoff strategies
- Cross-team governance and ownership
- Metrics: latency, payout SLA, MTTR, post-incident learning

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: simple circuit breaker
class Breaker {
  constructor(threshold) {
    this.failures = 0;
    this.threshold = threshold;
    this.open = false;
  }
  call(fn) {
    if (this.open) throw new Error('Breaker is open');
    return fn().catch(() => {
      this.failures++;
      if (this.failures > this.threshold) this.open = true;
      throw;
    });
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure success after the fix? 
- What would you include in the post-incident report for audit and compliance?
